  "id": "MUS_SEA",
  "title": "The sea",
  "about": "The music of the sea map by weather (Book 11 section 03, MUS_SEA_CALM/WIND/STORM; Stage 13, decisions S13-60 to S13-65): three pieces in one key and tempo, so a change of weather cross-fades on a shared bar grid. D Aeolian at 64 beats a minute in 4/4, sixteen bars (a minute) a pass, over a low drone re-struck every four bars so it never drops out, at the seam or anywhere else. The sea is vast and indifferent (section 01): a long echo, few instruments, dread rather than adventure. The calm: the drone, the rowing stroke on a soft frame drum (a stroke every two beats, as the crew pull), the oars creaking on the recovery, a pad held long like the wind in the sail, and a sparse harp far off with long silences; it avoids the sixth, so it sits between the launch's Dorian and the sea's Aeolian. The wind: the same rowing pulse and pad under a breathy flute carrying a long tune with cuts, darkening to the lowered sixth (Bb) in its middle. The storm: no tune; the drone, a deeper drone grinding a semitone between the lowered sixth and the fifth (Bb and A), driving frame drums in quavers, a great drum like a sea breaking every second bar, and a low choir pad. Each starts from the drone alone and its layers join one at a time on bar lines (Book 10 Music fades). Written for the game; no borrowed tune.",
